## Overview

This service handles the full lifecycle of payment reconciliation:

1. **Document Upload** — Accepts invoice or payment PDFs/images (up to 10 MB) via REST.
2. **LLM Extraction** — Extracts structured fields (amounts, dates, invoice numbers, customer info) using Groq and Google Gemini Vision, with retry logic and mismatch detection.
3. **Background Processing** — Extraction runs in an RQ worker queue so uploads return immediately with a `job_id`.
4. **Matching** — A configurable scoring pipeline matches payments to invoices across five strategies: invoice number, customer, currency, amount, and closes-balance.
5. **Aging & Reminders** — A scheduled job classifies overdue invoices by severity and sends email reminders based on configurable aging rules.
6. **WebSocket** — Real-time aging updates are pushed to connected clients.

---

## Architecture

```
Client
  │
  ▼
API Gateway
  │
  ├── FastAPI (this service)
  │     ├── /documents   — upload, status polling, CRUD
  │     ├── /matching    — scores, dashboard, discrepancies
  │     └── /aging-config, /scheduler — aging rules & reminders
  │
  ├── Redis
  │     ├── Job status cache  (key: job:<job_id>,     TTL 1h)
  │     └── Preview cache     (key: preview:<doc_id>, TTL 10m)
  │
  ├── RQ Worker (worker.py)
  │     └── process_document_task_sync → LLM extraction → DB write
  │
  ├── PostgreSQL
  │     ├── documents, invoice_data, payment_details
  │     ├── matching_payment_invoice
  │     ├── customers, aging_config, reminder_log
  │     └── scheduler_settings, exchange_rates
  │
  └── Google Cloud Storage
        └── Raw document files
```

---

## Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| API framework | FastAPI + Uvicorn |
| Database ORM | SQLAlchemy (async) + asyncpg |
| Migrations | Alembic + Flyway SQL scripts |
| Task queue | RQ (Redis Queue) |
| Cache | Redis (sync + async clients) |
| LLM — text | Groq (LangChain) |
| LLM — vision | Google Gemini Vision |
| File storage | Google Cloud Storage |
| Scheduler | APScheduler |
| Email | FastMail |
| Deployment | Google Cloud Run |

