## Local Setup

**Prerequisites:** Python 3.12+, PostgreSQL, Redis

```bash
# Clone and enter the service directory
cd payment_intake_matching_service

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Copy and fill in environment variables
cp .env.example .env
```

---

## Database Migrations

The service uses both Alembic (for the ORM schema) and Flyway SQL scripts under `src/api/migrations/`.

```bash
# Initialise Alembic (first time only)
alembic init alembic

# Set sqlalchemy.url in alembic.ini, or export DATABASE_URL and
# add this to alembic/env.py:
#   import os
#   config.set_main_option("sqlalchemy.url", os.environ["DATABASE_URL"])

# Stamp existing DB as up-to-date (if schema already exists)
python -m alembic stamp head

# Generate a new migration from model changes
python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"

# Apply migrations
python -m alembic upgrade head
```

SQL scripts in `src/api/migrations/` follow Flyway naming (`V1__...sql` through `V9__...sql`) and create the core tables: `aging_config`, `customers`, `documents`, `invoice_data`, `payment_details`, `matching_payment_invoice`, `reminder_log`, `scheduler_settings`, `exchange_rates`.

---

## Running the Service

```bash
# Development
uvicorn src.api.rest.app:app --reload --port 8000

# Production
uvicorn src.api.rest.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
```

Interactive API docs are available at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.

---

## Running the RQ Worker

The worker runs separately from the API. It exposes a `/health` endpoint on port 8080 for Cloud Run health checks.

```bash
python src/worker.py
```

The worker connects to the same Redis instance and processes jobs from the `default` queue. It uses `SimpleWorker` (single-threaded, no forking) — suitable for Cloud Run's single-process containers.

---

## API Endpoints

All endpoints are prefixed with `/api/v1/payment_intake_matching` and require a JWT Bearer token unless noted.

### Documents

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/documents/upload?document_type=INVOICE\|PAYMENT` | Upload a file; returns `job_id` immediately |
| `GET` | `/documents/jobs/{job_id}/status` | Poll extraction status (`PROCESSING`, `EXTRACTED`, `FAILED`) |
| `GET` | `/documents/` | List all documents |
| `GET` | `/documents/{document_id}` | Get a single document |
| `GET` | `/documents/{document_id}/invoices` | Get extracted invoices with match status |
| `GET` | `/documents/{document_id}/payments` | Get extracted payments |
| `POST` | `/documents/{document_id}/save` | Persist reviewed records to the database |
| `GET` | `/documents/stats` | Aggregate user statistics |
| `DELETE` | `/documents/invoices/{invoice_id}` | Soft-delete an invoice |
| `DELETE` | `/documents/payments/{payment_id}` | Soft-delete a payment |

### Matching

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/matching/payment/{payment_id}` | All matches for a payment |
| `GET` | `/matching/invoice/{invoice_id}` | All matches for an invoice |
| `GET` | `/matching/invoice-detail/{invoice_id}` | Full invoice detail with matches |
| `GET` | `/matching/payment-detail/{payment_id}` | Full payment detail with matches |
| `GET` | `/matching/dashboard/summary` | Matched / unmatched totals |
| `GET` | `/matching/dashboard/unmatched-payments` | Unmatched payments list |
| `GET` | `/matching/dashboard/unmatched-invoices` | Unmatched invoices list |
| `GET` | `/matching/dashboard/recent?limit=20` | Most recent matches |
| `GET` | `/matching/dashboard/discrepancies` | Amount discrepancies across matches |

### Aging & Reminders

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/aging/run` | Manually trigger the aging + reminder job |
| `GET` | `/aging-config/` | List all aging configs |
| `POST` | `/aging-config/` | Create an aging config |
| `GET` | `/aging-config/{config_id}` | Get a config |
| `PUT` | `/aging-config/{config_id}` | Update a config |
| `DELETE` | `/aging-config/{config_id}` | Delete a config |
| `GET` | `/aging/reminders` | List all reminder logs |
| `GET` | `/scheduler/settings` | Get scheduler settings |
| `PUT` | `/scheduler/settings` | Update scheduler time and enable/disable |
| `GET` | `/scheduler/status` | Live scheduler status and next run time |

### WebSocket

| Path | Description |
|---|---|
| `WS /ws/aging` | Real-time aging updates stream |

---

## Matching Pipeline

Payments are matched to invoices through a five-strategy scoring pipeline. Strategies run in order; any strategy can hard-disqualify a candidate (score drops to 0 immediately).

| Order | Strategy | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Invoice Number** | Hard-disqualifies if no invoice number overlap is found |
| 2 | **Customer** | Scores name similarity; penalises mismatches |
| 3 | **Currency** | Hard-disqualifies on currency mismatch; bonus for exact match |
| 4 | **Amount** | Scores how closely the payment covers the invoice amount |
| 5 | **Closes Balance** | Bonus if the payment exactly zeros out the outstanding balance |

Scores from all passing strategies are summed and capped at 100. Matches above the configured threshold are written to `matching_payment_invoice`.

---

## Deployment

The service is deployed to **Google Cloud Run** as two separate services:

- `paisavasool-paymentmatching-service` — the FastAPI API
- `paisavasool-rq-worker` — the RQ worker (`src/worker.py`)

Both services read environment variables from Cloud Run secret environment variables or the `.env` file at build time.

```bash
# Build and push image
docker build -t gcr.io/<project>/<image>:<tag> .
docker push gcr.io/<project>/<image>:<tag>

# Deploy API
gcloud run deploy paisavasool-paymentmatching-service \
  --image gcr.io/<project>/<image>:<tag> \
  --region us-east1 \
  --set-env-vars ENV=production

# Deploy Worker
gcloud run deploy paisavasool-rq-worker \
  --image gcr.io/<project>/<worker-image>:<tag> \
  --region us-east1 \
  --command "python,src/worker.py"
```

The worker's `/health` endpoint on port 8080 satisfies Cloud Run's startup and liveness probes.